cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Image & Video Compression Lab: A From-Scratch Hybrid Video Codec"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dhariwal"
    given-names: "Aakarsh"
    affiliation: "Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU)"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch implementation of a JPEG/MPEG-style hybrid video codec —
  block DCT transform coding, scalar quantization, zigzag scanning,
  run-level coding, Huffman entropy coding, block motion estimation and
  compensation, and an I-frame/P-frame hybrid coding structure — extended
  with half-pel motion estimation, rate-distortion-optimized coefficient
  decisions, and an H.264-style in-loop deblocking filter. Built for the
  "Image and Video Compression Lab Course", Lehrstuhl für
  Multimediakommunikation und Signalverarbeitung (LMS), FAU
  Erlangen-Nürnberg, Summer Term 2022.
date-released: "2022-07-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aakarshdhariwal/image-video-compression-lab"
keywords:
  - video coding
  - image compression
  - hybrid video codec
  - motion estimation
  - motion compensation
  - discrete cosine transform
  - quantization
  - huffman coding
  - rate-distortion optimization
  - deblocking filter
